 "observations": [
  "body: the figure fills the page under the first two lines; lines 3 to 31 and the two notes stand in a narrow column at its right, the notes under a short rule. The line numbers 5 to 30 stand in the right margin. The page has no locator.",
  "body: the figure is redrawn from measurements of the print: the circle of the Sun with its diameter AC, the ten discs of the Moon from N to F with their diameters KH and ML, the line from the top of the Sun through N and the Earth I to F, the small circle at I and the dotted half circle at the right are fitted to the printed ink; the lower half of each disc, which the print fills with close horizontal hatching, is hatched with lines 0.9 pt apart; the letters and the words (SOL, PARS OBSCURA, PARS ILLUSTRATA, TERRA and, upright, HOC HEMISPHAERIUM UT ALTERUM DESCRIBATUR.) stand where they are printed.",
  "body L6, L27: «tros KH signemus.» and «rium quod Terram» are set close, without the full spaces of the column.",
  "body L16: «circumferentias» is spaced out to fill the line of the column; it is not a letter-spaced name.",
  "body L31: a point stands low before «pars» and another above the space before it; neither is a sign.",
  "notes L1: the hyphen of «tangen-» is printed short, as a point at mid height."
 ],
